# Coding Standards

## No Duplicate Logic

- Never copy-paste utility functions across files. Extract to a shared module.
- Auth helpers go in `lib/server/auth.ts`, chat utilities in `lib/server/chat-utils.ts`.
- Shared UI patterns (modals, API key inputs) go in `components/shared/`.

## API Route Conventions

- Always import `getUserFromSession` from `@/lib/server/auth` for authentication.
- Always verify ownership (`chat.user_id === sessionUser.id`) before GET/PUT/DELETE on user-owned resources.
- Use `NextRequest` (not `Request`) for type safety. Derive redirect URLs from `request.url`, never hardcode `localhost`.
- Import `ChatMessage` and `foldSystemIntoUser` from `@/lib/server/chat-utils` — never redefine locally.

## Component Size Limits

- Components over 200 lines should be extracted into their own file (e.g., `SetupScreen` lives in `components/story/SetupScreen.tsx`, not inline in `page.tsx`).
- Context providers over 250 lines should decompose logic into custom hooks (e.g., `useStorySave`, `useStoryPrefetch`).

## React Patterns

- All hooks must be called before any early returns (`if (...) return null` must come after all `useCallback`/`useState`/etc.).
- Use `useCallback` for functions passed as props or used in `useEffect` dependencies.
- Prefer composition (small hooks composed in a provider) over monolithic context files.

## CSS

- One CSS module per component when the file exceeds ~100 lines of styles.
- Shared styles go in `components/shared/*.module.css`.
- Use CSS variables from `globals.css` — never hardcode colors.

## Types

- Remove unused type exports promptly. Don't let dead types accumulate.
- Import types from `@/lib/shared/types` — never redefine `ChatMessage` etc. locally in API routes.

## Temperature & Settings Consistency

- Temperature slider range must be 0-2 in both SettingsPanel and StorySettings.
